# Rust / Cargo
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
Cargo.lock.bak

# Python bytecode. The vendored graph-admission tools are Python, and running
# them writes `__pycache__/` beside them — which makes the working tree dirty
# and the admission gate refuse its own run with STALE_GRAPH.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Datarim workflow state (local, per File Sync Policy)
/datarim/

# Ephemeral docs (transient working material)
/docs/ephemeral/
/.mandate.md

# Build / dist artefacts
/dist/
/build/

# Logs
*.log

# Credentials — defence in depth (canonical store is Vault per CLAUDE.md)
*.pem
*.key
*.token
**/Credentials/**
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dev-tools/smoke/.out/

# Receipts of paid runs (`arcana run --work-item` writes them here).
#
# A `ReadinessReceipt/v1` committed into the tree is read by graph admission as
# a historical receipt — asserted, never re-verified — so it returns
# `not_measured` and the change it was meant to support is admitted
# `PAUSED_SAFE`. The evidence of a run belongs in the pull request and in the
# dispatcher's `runs/` directory. `receipts/graph/` is the opposite case and
# stays tracked: an admission receipt is a claim ABOUT a change, made at the
# commit that carries it.
/receipts/ReadinessReceipt-*.json
